{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960749,"nonce":"O3EaaC8drKPz2CDCmK3aB0xnBI8=","title":"move cb_window onto xwindow, as cb_gpu moved onto xgpu","message":"xwindow (github.com/rayzor-blade/xwindow) is the window core for Caribou, Ash and Rayzor, generated through x-idl the way xgpu is. Its events keep cb_window's shapes (`Event`, `KeyEvent.Input`, `PhysicalKey`, `Key`, `KeySupplement`, `Modifiers`, `FilePath` with exact bytes, `TouchForce`, `Ime`, `DeviceEvent`), now generated for every runtime. cb_window would keep only its adapter: `xwindow_bindgen::generate(Runtime::Caribou)`, `xwindow_backend::install`, `caribou_abi`'s carriers and the page files `xwindow.mjs` and `xwindow_wire.mjs`.\n\nA scratch adapter on caribou_abi builds natively and for wasm32-wasip1-threads; `caribou describe` lists `window.Window` and the nested `window.Event`.\n\nWhat changes for programs:\n\n- `WindowBuilder` becomes `WindowAttributes` (setters) and `Window.open(attributes)`; methods are camelCase (`setImeAllowed`).\n- The synchronous `on_scale_factor_changed` callback becomes `setScaleSizing(Logical | Physical)`.\n- `platform()` follows xgpu's table. cb_window's web backend reports 5, which xgpu reads as Android; xwindow reports 7, the web canvas.\n- In a page, xwindow's own agent replaces Ash's `window.mjs` block (ash_window), started as `host::agent(\"xwindow\", block)`.\n\nFixtures to move: plugins/fixtures/window and window_gpu, crates/caribou-interop's window_events plugin.","files":null}]}